All three queries compute the Wyoming share, but `0result.sql` is the most robust:

• Uses one pass over the table with conditional aggregation (no unnecessary join).  
• SAFE_DIVIDE prevents division‑by‑zero.  
• HAVING filters out names that never occur in WY.  
• The tie‑breaker (second ORDER‑BY column) prefers the larger Wyoming count, which is sensible if two names happened to share the same proportion.

Therefore `0result.sql` is the best choice.

```plaintext
0result.sql
```